Figures~\ref{u2_tau_plot} and, even more clearly, Fig.~\ref{u2_tau_plot2} show that as the Poisson's ratio $\nu$ increases, the nonlinear solution transitions from being more compliant to being stiffer than the linear one. In the incompressible limit $\nu \to 0.5$, the linear solution approaches a non-trivial deformation state, whereas the nonlinear solution tends toward the undeformed configuration.

The same conclusion drawn from the previous figures can also be inferred from Fig.~\ref{fig:disp}, which presents maps of the displacement magnitude plotted on the deformed coated disc system.

