\paragrapht{2D any point tracker.}
In order to associate multiple observations of an object across frames, we leverage CoTracker3~\cite{karaev2024cotracker3}. 
Given the instance mask of all the objects detected in each frame, we queried the 2D points within each instance mask to retrieve the corresponding tracked mask in other frames. 
We use publicly available weights, CoTracker3 online, for all the experiments, without fine-tuning. 

\paragrapht{Monocular depth estimators.}
We employ two zero-shot monocular metric-depth estimators in our experiments: UniDepth~\cite{unidepth} and DepthPro~\cite{depthpro}.
Based on our findings, UniDepth performs exceptionally well in driving scenes, while DepthPro is more suited for general environments.
This difference arises mainly from their training datasets -- UniDepth is trained on more outdoor datasets, primarily from driving scenarios (e.g., Waymo~\cite{waymo}, Argoverse2~\cite{Argoverse2}).
In contrast, DepthPro produces precise metric-depth estimates and captures fine local object details with less distortion, while it struggles on KITTI~\cite{kitti} due to the limited number of driving datasets in its training.
For these reasons, we primarily use UniDepth for KITTI and DepthPro for in-the-wild testing.
Notably, both models can estimate camera intrinsics, opening the possibility for future extensions that do not rely on ground-truth camera intrinsic.


