\section{Additional Results}
\label{B}
\subsection{Without GT intrinsics}
Recent single-image calibration methods \cite{jin2023perspective, veicht2024geocalib} and zero-shot depth estimation models \cite{depthpro, unidepth} have demonstrated robust focal length estimation across various camera models.
In Tab.\ref{tab:ablation_intrinsics}, we analyze the effect of using estimated focal length on pseudo-labeling accuracy in the KITTI~\cite{kitti} dataset.
The focal length and depth values are obtained from UniDepth~\cite{unidepth}, assuming the principal point is at the image center.
Per-frame focal length estimations are averaged across all frames for a single scene, reflecting the assumption of a consistent camera model.
Our results show that estimated focal length significantly affects scene-level localization accuracy, as indicated by higher ATE in the near region.
However, its impact on object-level estimations, such as dimensions and orientation, is minimal.

\subsection{Qualitative results on KITTI dataset.}
In Fig.~\ref{fig:supp_kitti_qual}, we also present additional qualitative results on the KITTI~\cite{kitti} dataset. Compared to OVM3D-Det~\cite{huangtraining}, our method reduces duplicate detections and provides more accurate center estimations.


