where $\Gamma = \mathbb{C}^{\Nbs} \times \mathbb{R}^{3 \Nbs}$ is the considered parameter space.

Assuming well-separated targets (cf. Section~\ref{sec:2ndStage}), we treat each \ac{RoI} as a single-target estimation problem and drop the subscript $l$ for clarity.  By ignoring those terms that are not relevant for the estimation and considering \eqref{eq:cartesian_to_polar}, the log-likelihood function of the received signal $\underline{\mathbf{y}}$ is given by  
