For a smooth monomial curve $R$,  $\widetilde{R}$ is the Veronese subring of $\mathcal{K}[s,t]$ generated by all monomials of degree $d$, so we have $l = 1$. It is also straightforward to verify that $R_2' \subseteq R_1 R_1'$ or $R_2' \subseteq R_2$. From \cite[Example 1.9]{6}, we know that $r_Q(\widetilde{R}) = 1$. Hence, by Corollary~\ref{corollary reg}, we obtain the desired result.
