\begin{abstract}
Based on extensive numerical evidence, a recent paper (Sheng Chen et al., Eur. J. Phys. {\bf 45} (2024), 045703) suggested that the potential of a uniformly charged rose-shaped disk in the plane of the disk has a simple asymptotic form. We present an analytical proof of this interesting conjecture.
\end{abstract}

